@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture;performance] universal-foliage-pipeline
Except for the bounded ordinary-prop category specified below, ALL current and future vegetation (trees, palms, bushes, hedges, flowers, grass,
groundcover and vegetation embedded in mixed meshes), in every region and import
namespace, MUST pass through foliage_system's build-time classification, bounded
representation generation and validation, and UYorimichiFoliageSubsystem at runtime.
New vegetation MUST declare recognizable foliage material/asset semantics or certified per-face roles; hiding
foliage inside an unclassified material or bypassing the registry is forbidden.
Name heuristics MUST match semantic words at delimiters/camel-case boundaries, including numbered
variants and regular plurals; a substring such as tree inside streets MUST NOT classify rigid geometry.
Build-time and runtime name rules MUST agree. Runtime audits MUST reuse unchanged classification
verdicts, including non-vegetation, and invalidate them on mesh, material or role-slot changes.
Authored visibility changes to managed components MUST go through the foliage owner so the current
renderers and the state restored by switching modes agree.
Explicit rigid role certification is only for non-vegetation surfaces (such as fruit reusing leaf paint),
never an exemption for vegetation or an optimization fallback.
Non-vegetation collision helpers MAY be disambiguated from the name-only heuristic
only through an exact hard StaticMesh complex_collision_mesh reference. Explicit
foliage roles/material semantics MUST win. This MUST NOT add rigid stamps or runtime
exemptions; naming a mesh Collision alone proves nothing.
Missing, stale or invalid representations MUST fail the normal build and gameplay
readiness, never silently render an unoptimized fallback. Preparation and all cooked
dependencies MUST belong to the normal incremental build graph.
The persistent graphics switch MUST restore the original rendering when disabled;
both modes MUST remain managed by the same subsystem. Optimized play MUST load only prepared meshes;
legacy meshes MUST load only when explicitly selected. Switching MAY reload assets and MUST release the
inactive mesh set before loading its replacement, preserving placements, camera visibility and gameplay
without a restart. Prepared trees MUST provide simple trunk collision with passable foliage; mixed
meshes MUST preserve solid ground/building collision. Bush interaction MUST remain active.
Certified distant rigid LODs MAY contain zero faces; the runtime reader MUST accept them while
requiring positive LOD0 exactly matching the carrier and refusing negative or fractional counts.
Resident canopy meshes MUST retain the complete bounded authored LOD chain (one to eight levels),
including distant impostors and their native screen thresholds. Trees with multiple authored levels
MUST retain a matching rigid chain. A tree with one authored level MAY reuse that single rigid level
across its generated leaf reductions; mixed rigid carriers MAY also use one level. Only a source
with no lower authored LOD MAY use generated leaf reductions. Exact empty distant canopy levels MAY be retained, but
LOD0 MUST remain positive and every saved/rendered count MUST match the receiving proof.
Small authored plant props with a complete FoliageAuthored_ slot table and 1–12,288
LOD0 triangles MUST stay on the ordinary prop path in both graphics modes, preserving
their existing rendering and collision without replacement meshes. This explicit
export-certified exception MUST NOT exclude dense vegetation, partial role tables,
oversized meshes or unclassified sources. Cached verdicts MUST invalidate on triangle-count changes.
Visual and shadow representations MUST have separate budgets; distant forest patches
MUST preserve silhouettes and clearings. Changes MUST carry revision-bound ground,
canopy and aerial captures plus real-time frame/GPU timings before performance or
visual-equivalence claims. Detached cosmetic particles are not vegetation placements.
@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture;performance] foliage-native-preparation-boundary
Foliage geometry preparation, palette export and snapshot readback MUST live in the
YorimichiFoliagePreparation editor module, independently of raw import role certification in
YorimichiImport. Neither module MAY link the other. The preparation owner MUST declare its own
module digest; raw imports MUST NOT depend on that digest. A preparation-only compiled change
MUST preserve raw import keys when their real source, engine, configuration and module bytes are unchanged.
